        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"Veet\"]\n\nI actually kind of figuired the H scaling effect might be balanced out by the fact that they wouldn&#39;t have their secondary effect go off every turn like the others.\n\n[/quote]\n\nThe problem is though that it results in double scaling. &nbsp;Playing against the V5 already scales, because you&#39;re playing against (H) V5 decks. &nbsp;If one of the members has damage that scales with (H), then that individual member becomes tougher or easier, in addition to having more partners. &nbsp;Now, if you want to make the Ennead member harder, you can fix (H) as higher (always 4, always 5), but you really don&#39;t want it to actually fluctuate with (H).\n",
